# Reject hunt — attach before miss

**Product law:** On write-reject / API-error locate (`isApiRejectAsk`), consume a relevant **search hit snippet** as a retrieval lead instead of repeating searches or ignoring it. Preserve the selected repo/ref and the snippet's provenance. A search snippet is not an opened remote body, verified surrounding behavior or an exact-source live Pass; attempt the relevant remote read before asserting those stronger claims.

## Fail class this blocks (2026-09-29 dogfood)

Exact Parent ValidationError ask on indexed `plane` / `preview`:

| What happened | Why |
|---------------|-----|
| 10× `search_code`, **0** `read_file` | Ranking emptied `preferredHits`; auto-read only follows preferred |
| Index hit already had the raise line | Snippet never treated as attachable evidence |
| Canned miss | Finish assumed “no body read” = no evidence |

Earlier rules covered **right file, wrong floor** (opened serializer → must jump in-file before miss). They did **not** cover **hit already is the raise, never opened**.

## Required behavior

| Evidence state | Must do |
|----------------|---------|
| Search hit content matches asked-field write-reject **or** the exact error string the user quoted (Zoekt often returns only that line — no `raise` / `ValidationError`) | Retain/attach the snippet as a labeled lead immediately, then attempt the relevant remote body/window. If fetch fails, preserve the lead and state the verification limit |
| `preferredHits` would be empty but hits include server write / reject snippet | Keep those hits in `preferredHits` — never discard the whole pool on reject |
| Preferred / server-write path opened, window lacks reject | In-file jump / fuller read **before** miss |
| No relevant lead or verified reject after soft gather | Short honest limit. Distinguish not found from found-in-search-but-body-unavailable; do not invent a verified result |

## Hard fails (never ship)

| Reject | Prefer |
|--------|--------|
| More `search_code` while a hit already contains the asked ValidationError | Consume the lead → remote read → answer within verified scope |
| Empty `preferredHits` on reject when original hits had serializers/raise lines | Retain actionable hits without relaxing authorization or verification |
| Canned miss with 0 reads after Zoekt returned the raise | Attach or jump first |
| Losing a useful lead when remote read fails, or calling snippet-only attachment verified success | Preserve labeled lead; keep the required remote-body/source gate open |
| Unit tests that only mock happy-path body fetch | Regression: hit has raise + `readRemoteFile` → `undefined` → retain search-snippet provenance, but fail the verified-body gate |

## Implementation choke

- `AgentOrchestrator`: after `search_code` on reject, `attachRejectFromSearchHits` / `attachRejectSnippetPayload` before more searches
- `decorateToolResult`: reject must not zero out `preferredHits` when actionable hits exist
- Finish: consume actionable leads; do not conflate ignored evidence with no evidence. A snippet-only result does not satisfy the existing remotely verified evidence gate.

## Self-check

Would Exact Parent ignore a relevant hit, or claim remotely verified behavior when the body fetch is empty? Either fails. Preserve the lead and the honest unavailable boundary; qualify the actual remote/body/publication path before declaring live Pass.
